# Ice Cauldron activated for X = 0 exiles a Lightning Bolt and notes no mana: tapped for mana two turns later, it adds
# nothing (the ruling: "X can be zero. This places a zero mana counter on the Cauldron"). Activated again for X = 3, paid
# {R}{R}{R}, Bot1 exiles nothing though a second Lightning Bolt is in hand ("you may"): the counter is still put and the
# mana noted (CR 607.2e), and the last card exiled with the Cauldron is still the first Bolt (CR 607.2a) - so its mana,
# {R}{R}{R}, may be spent on that Bolt from exile, not on the one in hand (CR 106.6).
